From b09ad8faaf1f9ec57841280b5af8e348a732bd82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:49:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] asahi/drm-shim: model the M5 Pro kernel's submission
 checks

The noop shim's G17S identity reports only the program storage features
and accepts every submission, so a driver that submits renders the M5
Pro kernel refuses works offline and fails only on the machine: the
Gallium driver's every render was refused there with EINVAL at the G17
runtime's prepare_command (g17/runtime/backend.rs), and nothing offline
showed it.

Add ASAHI_SHIM_CHIP=g17s-kernel, the M5 Pro as the G17 kernel runtime
presents it (GET_PARAMS of the E2 kernel on a J716s: features
0x23cfe7c06 less the VM status and independent queue bits, whose ioctls
the shim does not emulate by default; revision 17, two clusters of ten
cores), and an M5 submission gate it applies to every submit. The gate
replicates the kernel's structural checks: the command parser (barriers,
software commands, command count), the render and compute command
validation of the M5 command set (allowed flags, dimensions, utiles,
samples, the 64 KiB tile buffer, no sampler heap, no helper programs,
background and end-of-tile programs present), the program storage lists
and their per-entry demand limits, the render-requires-a-list rule and
the M5 render admission, including the compressed multisample
depth/stencil forms when the kernel reports them. It does not model the
pool budget, the address space or the firmware. A refusal returns the
kernel's errno and names the check.

ASAHI_SHIM_M5_GATE=1 applies the gate to any HAL300 identity, =warn only
reports, =0 turns it off; ASAHI_SHIM_M5_EXPECT_VALID fails the run at
exit if anything was refused. Honeykrisp's submissions pass it (vkmark
headless: 470k submissions, none refused).

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM Claude
---
